course: dictionary
lesson: 5085
title: Insurgent: who is fighting whom?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An insurgent is a person who fights against the people in charge of their country, often with weapons. Look for clues in the sentence: «The Ukrainian Insurgent Army fought for independence against Soviet forces.» Fighting against forces that control a country tells you the insurgents were rising up against a ruling power.
explain: Insurgent can also be a describing word, an adjective. An insurgent group is a group that rebels against those in power. In politics, an insurgent campaign is a new challenger rising against the established leaders.
explain: The same people can be called different things. Insurgent, rebel and freedom fighter may describe one group, but each word can show how the writer feels about them. A careful reader asks: who chose this word, and why?
fact: An insurgent is a person who fights against the government or ruling power of their country.
fact: As an adjective, insurgent means rebelling or rising up against those in power.
fact: In politics, an insurgent is a new challenger rising against an old leader.
fact: «Insurgent» and «rebel» can describe the same people, so the word a writer chooses can show their view.
fact: «The Ukrainian Insurgent Army fought for independence against Soviet forces.»
exercise: «The insurgents fought against the government of their country.» What is an insurgent? | A teacher who sets homework | *A person who fights against the people in charge | A person who runs a shop | A king who rules peacefully
exercise: In an election, a new party challenges the leaders who have ruled for years. Which word fits this new challenger? | Luminous | Ancient | Famished | *Insurgent
exercise: As an adjective, what does «insurgent» mean? | Giving out light | Very old | Very hungry | *Rebelling against those in power
test: «The Ukrainian Insurgent Army fought for independence.» Independence means | Being short and rude | Being hungry for food | Being wet and grey | *Being free to govern itself
test: One writer calls a fighter an insurgent, and another calls the same fighter a freedom fighter. Why might they choose different words? | Both words mean exactly the same to every reader | *Each word can show a different view of the same people | Words never change their meaning | One writer made a spelling mistake
exam: In «Insurgent groups fought for power against the leaders», which clue shows that insurgent means rebelling? | The number of words in the sentence | *The words fought for power against the leaders | The word for | The word groups
